1.0 Introduction
1.1 Purpose
This LLD describes implementation-level details for the Authenticator mobile application (Flutter). It expands the HLD into concrete modules, classes, methods, data contracts, validations, events, triggers, and algorithms so developers can code and testers can derive cases with full traceability.
1.2 Scope

MVP scope: account setup (QR/manual), secure storage of secrets, offline TOTP generation (6 digits, 30s), OTP display with countdown, clipboard copy with 30s auto-clear, screen-capture protection, optional app lock, and error handling.

1.3 Assumptions and Dependencies
•	Device time is accurate; OS provides secure storage (Keychain/Keystore).
•	Flutter SDK with packages: camera, google_mlkit_barcode_scanning, flutter_secure_storage, crypto, base32, permission_handler, provider.
        1.4 Intended audience
Developers, architects, QA, SEPG reviewers.
          1.5 References
	SRS Document.
	High Level Design Document				
2.0 Procedure
      2.1 Priority Level	
		High (MVP) unless stated otherwise.
	
       2.2 Design Consideration
Reuse and Buy vs. Build Analysis:
•	Reuse/Buy: QR scanning (camera + ML Kit), secure storage, base32/crypto.
•	Build: TOTP engine glue code, URI parser, ViewModels, UI, clipboard auto-clear logic.
      2.3 Task Name
 Process Description
Scan QR → parse otpauth URI → validate fields → persist encrypted account JSON in secure storage → refresh UI list.
 
2.3.1  Entry Criteria
•	Camera permission granted; camera available.
•	Scanner screen active; ML Kit initialized.
2.3.1.1	Work Flow/ Data Flow Diagram
1) Open camera
2) Frame capture
3) ML Kit QR detect
4) Extract URI
5) Validate & parse
6) Persist encrypted JSON in secure storage
7) Notify ViewModel to refresh list.
 
2.3.1.2	List of Sub Tasks
Parse OTPAuth URI
Process Description
Extract scheme, label, and params: secret, issuer, accountName, algorithm (default SHA1), digits (default 6), period (default 30). Validate presence and format 
2.3.2  User Interface 
Screen: “Scan QR” with camera preview, overlay, Cancel. Error dialogs for invalid QR or permission denied.
 
2.3.3 Functions/ Objects / Scripts

class QRScanService {{ Future<String?> scanQRCode(); }}
class OtpAuthParser {{ ParsedAccount parse(String uri); }}

2.3.3.1	Method Signatures & Public APIs
This subsection lists public method signatures for major classes, their parameters, return types, and brief behavior notes. Use Dart-style signatures to match implementation.

## EncryptionService
class EncryptionService {
  Future<String> encrypt(String plainText, {String? associatedData});
  Future<String> decrypt(String encryptedText, {String? associatedData});
  Future<void> clearEncryptionKey();
  Future<String> encryptWithPassword(String plainText, String password);
  Future<String> decryptWithPassword(String encryptedText, String password);
  String? validatePassword(String password);
  String? getPasswordWarning(String password);
  Future<Map<String, dynamic>> getStorageInfo();
}

Note: Uses XChaCha20-Poly1305 AEAD for encryption. Master key stored in flutter_secure_storage with automatic hardware backing. Password-based encryption uses Argon2id KDF (64MB, 3 iterations, 4 parallelism) for backups.

---

## SecureStorageService
class SecureStorageService {
  Future<void> saveSecret(String key, String value);
  Future<String?> getSecret(String key);
  Future<void> deleteSecret(String key);
  Future<void> clearAllSecrets();
}

Note: Wrapper over flutter_secure_storage with platform-specific options (hardware-backed encryption on Android Keystore and iOS Keychain).

---

## DatabaseService
class DatabaseService {
  Future<List<Account>> getAllAccounts();
  Future<void> addAccount(Account account);
  Future<void> updateAccount(Account account);
  Future<void> deleteAccount(String accountId);
  Future<bool> accountExists(String issuer, String accountName);
  Future<Account?> getAccountByIssuerAndName(String issuer, String accountName);
  Future<void> close();
  Future<void> clearAllAccounts();
  Future<bool> verifyIntegrity();
}

Note: Stores accounts with secretKey encrypted via EncryptionService before writing to SQLite. Provides unique constraint handling, integrity verification, and migration hooks.

