2.3.4 Data Model / Table Description 

Secure Storage JSON (per account): id(UUID), issuer, accountName, secretKey, algorithm=SHA1, digits=6, period=30, createdAt(epoch).
2.3.5 Dependency               
mobile_scanner, permission_handler, flutter_secure_storage, cryptography, crypto, base32, bcrypt, sqflite, local_auth, safe_device, file_picker, share_plus, path_provider, font_awesome_flutter, qr_flutter, flutter_markdown, shared_preferences.
2.3.6 Field Level Validation
•	issuer not empty; accountName not empty.
•	secret Base32 valid; digits in {{6,8}}; period > 0.
•	Reject duplicate (issuer, accountName).
2.3.7 Event Description   
•	Scan starts camera.
•	On QR detected: parse; show confirm.
•	Save persists and navigates back.
2.3.8 Triggers       
•	Frame timer for periodic ML scanning (~1s).          
2.3.9  Business Rules   
•	Process QR to persist within ≤ 3 seconds.
•	On failure: show error; offer manual entry.
2.3.10 Algorithm Used  
•	URI parser; default handling; sanitization.
    

function parseOtpauth(uri):
  ensure uri.scheme == 'otpauth'
  extract type = 'totp'
  parse query parameters
  validate secret is Base32
  assign defaults (algorithm=SHA1, digits=6, period=30)
  return ParsedAccount






function generateTOTP(secret, time, digits, period, algorithm):
    counter = floor(time / period)
    key = decodeBase32(secret)
    hmac = HMAC(algorithm, key, counter)
    offset = lastNibble(hmac)
    binary = (hmac[offset:offset+4] & 0x7FFFFFFF)
    otp = binary mod (10^digits)
    return otp padded to digits



2.3.11 App Lock Logic / Secure Access Module

Implements optional app lock using biometric authentication or fallback PIN to secure access to the Authenticator app.
Uses local_auth for biometric APIs and stores hashed PIN securely in flutter_secure_storage.

Workflow:
1.	On app start/resume, check if lock is enabled.
2.	If enabled, prompt biometric → if fails, fallback to PIN entry.
3.	On success, navigate to dashboard; on failure after 3 attempts, exit app.
Dependencies:

local_auth, flutter_secure_storage, provider.

Pseudocode:

onAppLaunch():
    if lockEnabled:
        success = authWithBiometric() or verifyPin()
        if not success:
            exitApp()

2.3.12 Exception Handling and Error Codes


AuthService
- AUTH_PIN_INCORRECT — PIN verification failed (bcrypt mismatch) — UI: "Invalid PIN." show remaining attempts; Retry: allow retry until lockout.
- AUTH_TOO_MANY_ATTEMPTS — Max failed PIN attempts reached and lockout applied — UI: "Account locked. Try again in X minutes." (show countdown); Retry: disallow PIN attempts until lockout ends.
- AUTH_LOCKED — Attempt when locked (lockout still active) — UI: same as above; Retry: none until expiry.
- AUTH_BIOMETRIC_NOT_AVAILABLE — Biometric not enrolled or device doesn't support it — UI: "Biometric not available. Use PIN."; Retry: none; offer fallback to PIN setup.
- AUTH_BIOMETRIC_FAILED — Biometric auth rejected/cancelled/failed — UI: "Biometric failed or cancelled"; Retry: allow retry; recommend PIN fallback.
- AUTH_INTERNAL_ERROR — Unexpected auth error (platform API exceptions) — UI: "Authentication error. Try again."; Retry: allow few retries; log telemetry.

EncryptionService
- ENC_ENCRYPTION_FAILED — Encryption pipeline error — UI: "Internal error while saving secret"; Retry: allow one retry; log details.
- ENC_DECRYPTION_FAILED — Decryption failed (invalid format or key mismatch) — UI: "Unable to read secret"; Retry: none; mark account as unreadable.
- ENC_INVALID_FORMAT — Stored value doesn't match expected envelope format — UI: "Corrupted data"; Retry: none; log and surface option to remove corrupted account.
- ENC_KEY_ACCESS_FAILED — Failed to obtain encryption key from secure storage — UI: "Security error. Restart app."; Retry: retry once; if persistent, suggest device restart.
- ENC_KEY_GENERATION_FAILED — Failed to generate new encryption key — UI: "Failed to initialize security"; Retry: none; critical error requiring app reinstall.
- ENC_AUTHENTICATION_FAILED — AEAD authentication failed (data tampered) — UI: "Authentication failed - data may be tampered"; Retry: none; security critical.
- ENC_INCORRECT_PASSWORD — Password-based decryption failed (wrong password) — UI: "Incorrect password or corrupted data"; Retry: allow multiple retries.

Secure Storage
- STORAGE_IO_ERROR — Read/write to secure storage failed (I/O or OS-level error) — UI: "Storage error"; Retry: retry a couple of times; ask user to restart app/device if persists; log with platform details.

DatabaseService / AccountService
- DB_CONFLICT_ACCOUNT_EXISTS — Unique constraint violation when adding account — UI: "Account already exists"; Retry: none (offer edit or choose different account name).
- DB_WRITE_FAILED — Generic DB write failure — UI: "Failed to save"; Retry: retry once; if persists, instruct user to restart or export data.
- DB_READ_FAILED — DB read error / corrupted DB — UI: "Failed to load accounts"; Retry: none or limited; log and offer recovery/drain option.
- DB_INTEGRITY_FAILED — Database checksum mismatch (tampering detected) — UI: "Database integrity check failed"; Retry: none; log for security audit.

BackupService
- BACKUP_PASSWORD_WEAK — Password doesn't meet minimum requirements — UI: "Password must be at least 6 characters"; Retry: allow immediate retry with stronger password.
- BACKUP_FILE_NOT_FOUND — Backup file doesn't exist at specified path — UI: "File not found. The backup file could not be found."; Retry: allow user to select different file.
- BACKUP_INVALID_FORMAT — File is not a valid backup format — UI: "Invalid backup file. This file may be corrupted or not a valid backup."; Retry: none; suggest creating new backup.
- BACKUP_DECRYPTION_FAILED — Failed to decrypt backup (wrong password or corrupted) — UI: "Incorrect password or corrupted data"; Retry: allow multiple password attempts.
- BACKUP_CREATION_FAILED — Failed to create backup file — UI: "Failed to create backup"; Retry: retry once; check storage permissions and available space.

GoogleAuthImportService / AppExportService
- IMPORT_INVALID_URI — Not a valid otpauth-migration:// URI — UI: "Invalid QR code. Please scan a Google Authenticator export QR."; Retry: allow rescan.
- IMPORT_PARSE_FAILED — Failed to parse protobuf data — UI: "Failed to parse migration data"; Retry: allow rescan; may be corrupted QR.
- IMPORT_NO_ACCOUNTS — Migration URI contains no accounts — UI: "No accounts found in QR code"; Retry: allow rescan.
- EXPORT_EMPTY_LIST — Attempted to export empty account list — UI: "No accounts selected for export"; Retry: none; prompt user to select accounts.

SecurityService
- SECURITY_CHECK_FAILED — Device security check encountered error — UI: none (graceful degradation); Log: error details for debugging.
- SECURITY_DEVICE_ROOTED — Device is rooted/jailbroken — UI: "Warning: Device is rooted. Security may be compromised."; Retry: none; allow user to proceed or exit.
- SECURITY_EMULATOR_DETECTED — Running on emulator — UI: "Warning: Running on emulator"; Retry: none; allow in debug mode only.
- SECURITY_DEV_MODE — Developer mode enabled — UI: "Warning: Developer mode is enabled"; Retry: none; informational only.

IntegrityService
- INTEGRITY_CHECKSUM_MISMATCH — Database checksum doesn't match baseline — UI: "Database integrity check failed"; Retry: none; log for security audit; offer to recalculate baseline.
- INTEGRITY_CALCULATION_FAILED — Failed to calculate checksum — UI: none (silent failure); Log: error details; continue operation.

TOTP / QR parsing
- TOTP_INVALID_SECRET — Provided secret cannot be decoded (bad base32) — UI: "Invalid secret"; Retry: allow user to re-enter or rescan QR.
- QR_INVALID_URI — QR/scanned URI not an otpauth URI or missing mandatory params — UI: "Invalid QR code"; Retry: allow rescan and show hints on expected format.

Migration
- MIGRATE_LEGACY_KEY_PRESENT — Legacy raw AES key found during startup migration — Cause: app updated from older version — UI: none (migration background) ; Handling: attempt wrap+store, securely delete legacy key on success, log migration result.
- MIGRATE_WRAP_FAILED — Wrapping legacy key failed — UI: "Failed to upgrade secure storage"; Handling: retry once and escalate to telemetry; do not delete legacy key until wrapped copy verified.


